# Platform Notes

crossroot targets Windows (Git Bash), macOS, and Linux equally.

## Windows

### Requirements

- **Git for Windows** (includes Git Bash): https://git-scm.com/downloads
- **uv**: `winget install astral-sh.uv` or `powershell -c "irm https://astral.sh/uv/install.ps1 | iex"`
{% if include_typescript %}
- **{{ typescript_package_manager }}**: see https://{% if typescript_package_manager == "pnpm" %}pnpm.io/installation{% elif typescript_package_manager == "bun" %}bun.sh{% else %}nodejs.org{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if include_java %}
- **JDK 21+**: https://adoptium.net/
{% endif %}

### PATH Setup

Run all scripts in **Git Bash** (not PowerShell or CMD). After `croot bootstrap`, add `scripts/` to your Git Bash PATH:

```bash
# Append to ~/.bash_profile (not ~/.bashrc on Windows):
export PATH="$PATH:/d/src/{{ repo_slug }}/scripts"
```

Restart Git Bash or run `source ~/.bash_profile`.

### Notes

- Use forward slashes in paths inside scripts.
- `uv` installs to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\uv\bin`; ensure that's on your system PATH for GUI tools.

## macOS

```bash
# Install uv
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh

# Ensure ~/.local/bin is in PATH (uv installer advises this)
echo 'export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"' >> ~/.zshrc
```

## Linux

```bash
# Install uv
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh
```

Works with bash and zsh. Ensure `~/.local/bin` is in `PATH`.
